---

# NativeWind v4 — Complete Reference

NativeWind brings Tailwind CSS to React Native. On native it compiles to `StyleSheet.create`; on web it reuses the Tailwind CSS stylesheet. This project uses **NativeWind v4** with **Tailwind CSS v3**.

---

## Setup (Current Project)

### metro.config.js
```js
const { withNativeWind } = require("nativewind/metro");
module.exports = withNativeWind(config, { input: "./global.css" });
```

### babel.config.js
```js
module.exports = function (api) {
  api.cache(true);
  return {
    presets: [
      ["babel-preset-expo", { jsxImportSource: "nativewind" }],
      "nativewind/babel",
    ],
  };
};
```

### tailwind.config.js
```js
module.exports = {
  content: ["./app/**/*.{js,ts,tsx}", "./components/**/*.{js,ts,tsx}"],
  presets: [require("nativewind/preset")],
  theme: { extend: {} },
  plugins: [],
};
```

### global.css
```css
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;
```

### TypeScript — nativewind-env.d.ts
```ts
/// <reference types="nativewind/types" />
```
> Do NOT name this file `nativewind.d.ts` or match any folder name in node_modules.

---

## Core Concepts

### Explicit Styles (IMPORTANT)
React Native has issues with conditionally applied styles. Always declare both states:
```tsx
// ❌ Only dark mode color — broken on React Native
<Text className="dark:text-white" />

// ✅ Both light and dark declared
<Text className="text-black dark:text-white" />
```

### Colors Don't Cascade from View to Text
```tsx
// ❌ View does not accept `color` and won't cascade
<View className="text-red-500"><Text>Hello</Text></View>

// ✅ Color on the Text element
<View><Text className="text-red-500">Hello</Text></View>
```

### Platform Modifiers
```tsx
<Text className="ios:font-bold android:font-normal web:underline native:italic" />
```
Supported: `ios:`, `android:`, `web:`, `windows:`, `osx:`, `native:`.

### Flex Defaults Differ from Web
React Native defaults: `flexDirection: column`, `alignContent: flex-start`, `flexShrink: 0`.
Fix: always set `flex-1` and explicit `flex-row` / `flex-col`.

### dp vs px
React Native uses dp; web uses px. NativeWind treats them as equivalent.
Use `px` units in config/theme values — NativeWind normalises them.

### rem sizing
NativeWind uses `rem = 14` on native, `rem = 16` on web for consistency.
Override via `withNativeWind(config, { inlineRem: 16 })`.

---

## States & Pseudo-classes

| Modifier | Activating event | Deactivating event |
|---|---|---|
| `hover:` | `onHoverIn` | `onHoverOut` |
| `active:` | `onPressIn` | `onPressOut` |
| `focus:` | `onFocus` | `onBlur` |
| `disabled:` | `disabled={true}` prop | — |
| `empty:` | no children | — |

```tsx
<Pressable className="bg-blue-500 active:bg-blue-700">
  <Text className="text-white">Press Me</Text>
</Pressable>

<TextInput className="border disabled:opacity-50 disabled:bg-gray-200" disabled={disabled} />
```

> The component must support the event prop. `hover:` needs `onHoverIn`/`onHoverOut` — available on `Pressable` and `TextInput`, NOT on `View` or `Text`.

### Parent State (group)
```tsx
<Pressable className="group/card">
  <View className="group-active/card:bg-blue-100">
    <Text className="group-active/card:text-blue-700">
      Press the card
    </Text>
  </View>
</Pressable>
```

### Data Attribute Selectors
```tsx
<View
  className="[&[data-active]]:bg-green-500 [&[data-active='false']]:bg-gray-500"
  {...{ dataSet: { active: active } }}
/>
```

---

## Dark Mode

### Automatic (system preference) — default
In `app.json` set `"userInterfaceStyle": "automatic"` for Expo.
No Tailwind config change needed. Use `dark:` modifiers directly.

### Manual toggle — requires `darkMode: "class"` in tailwind.config
```js
// tailwind.config.js
module.exports = { darkMode: "class", ... };
```

```tsx
import { useColorScheme } from "nativewind";

function ThemeToggle() {
  const { colorScheme, toggleColorScheme, setColorScheme } = useColorScheme();
  return (
    <Pressable onPress={toggleColorScheme}>
