## Part 5 — HostObjects

HostObjects expose full C++ classes to JavaScript — an object with methods, not just a standalone function.

```cpp
class AudioPipelineHostObject : public jsi::HostObject {
public:
    explicit AudioPipelineHostObject(/* deps */) { /* init */ }
    ~AudioPipelineHostObject() override { /* RAII cleanup */ }

    // Called when JS reads obj.propertyName
    jsi::Value get(jsi::Runtime& rt, const jsi::PropNameID& name) override {
        std::string propName = name.utf8(rt);

        if (propName == "start") {
            return jsi::Function::createFromHostFunction(rt, name, 0,
                [this](jsi::Runtime& rt, const jsi::Value&,
                       const jsi::Value*, size_t) -> jsi::Value {
                    start();
                    return jsi::Value::undefined();
                });
        }
        if (propName == "volume") {
            return jsi::Value(volume_);
        }
        return jsi::Value::undefined();
    }

    // Called when JS writes obj.propertyName = value
    void set(jsi::Runtime& rt, const jsi::PropNameID& name,
             const jsi::Value& value) override {
        if (name.utf8(rt) == "volume") {
            volume_ = value.asNumber();
        }
    }

private:
    double volume_ = 1.0;
    void start() { /* ... */ }
};
```

**Installing a HostObject:**

```cpp
void install(jsi::Runtime& rt) {
    auto obj = std::make_shared<AudioPipelineHostObject>();
    auto jsObj = jsi::Object::createFromHostObject(rt, obj);
    rt.global().setProperty(rt, "AudioPipeline", std::move(jsObj));
}
```

**From JavaScript:**
```js
AudioPipeline.start();
AudioPipeline.volume = 0.8;
```

---

## Part 6 — Memory Ownership

Two memory systems with different rules:

| System | Manages | Freed by |
|--------|---------|---------|
| GC (Hermes Hades) | JS objects, HostObject wrappers | GC finalizer on JS thread |
| Native heap | C++ objects, buffers | C++ destructors (RAII) |

**The boundary:** A `jsi::Object` backed by a HostObject — the JSI runtime holds a `shared_ptr<HostObject>`. When JS drops all references, GC runs `finalizeUnreachableObjects`, which drops the `shared_ptr`. If the ref count hits zero, the HostObject destructor runs on the JS thread.

**Ownership pitfalls:**

| Pattern | Risk | Fix |
|---------|------|-----|
| Background thread holds raw ptr to HostObject member | Use-after-free when GC collects | `shared_ptr` co-ownership |
| Lambda `[this]` from HostObject dispatched to bg thread | Dangling `this` | `[self = shared_from_this()]` |
| `CallInvoker` callback captures `jsi::Value` | Value invalidated before callback runs | Copy data to C++ types before dispatching |
| `shared_ptr` cycle (A owns B, B owns A) | Memory leak — never freed | Break with `weak_ptr` |
| Large native alloc invisible to GC | OOM (GC doesn't know to collect) | Call `runtime.instrumentation().collectGarbage()` as hint |

---

## Part 7 — Platform Wiring

### iOS (Objective-C++ / CocoaPods)

**File extension:** `.mm` (Objective-C++) to mix ObjC and C++.

```objc
// ios/AudioModule.mm
#import "AudioModule.h"
#import <React/RCTBridge+Private.h>
#import <jsi/jsi.h>
#include "install.h"  // your C++ install()

@implementation AudioModule

RCT_EXPORT_MODULE()

- (void)setBridge:(RCTBridge *)bridge {
    // Runs after bridge init, before JS evaluation
    RCTCxxBridge *cxxBridge = (RCTCxxBridge *)bridge;
    if (cxxBridge.runtime) {
        install(*(facebook::jsi::Runtime *)cxxBridge.runtime);
    }
}

@end
```

**Podspec** (`AudioModule.podspec`):
```ruby
s.source_files = "ios/**/*.{h,m,mm}", "cpp/**/*.{h,cpp}"
s.dependency "React-Core"
s.dependency "React-jsi"
```

**Runtime source (iOS):** `RCTCxxBridge` — cast `cxxBridge.runtime` to `jsi::Runtime*`.

**Gotcha:** Never send an ObjC message (`[obj method]`) from a real-time audio callback — the ObjC runtime lock causes priority inversion. Use pure C/C++ in real-time threads.

### Android (JNI + CMake)

**CMakeLists.txt:**
```cmake
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.13)
project(audio)

add_library(audio SHARED
    cpp/install.cpp
    cpp/AudioPipelineHostObject.cpp
    cpp/TxRingBuffer.cpp
)

target_include_directories(audio PRIVATE
    ${REACT_NATIVE_DIR}/ReactCommon/jsi
    ${REACT_NATIVE_DIR}/ReactCommon
)

target_link_libraries(audio log android)

# ABI filter — include all targets
# In build.gradle: abiFilters "armeabi-v7a", "arm64-v8a", "x86", "x86_64"
```

**Kotlin companion object:**
```kotlin
class AudioModule(reactContext: ReactApplicationContext) :
    ReactContextBaseJavaModule(reactContext) {

    companion object {
        init {
            System.loadLibrary("audio")  // loads libaudio.so
        }
    }

    // Called from JNI — entry point for install()
    external fun nativeInstall(jsiPtr: Long)

    override fun initialize() {
        super.initialize()
        val jsContext = reactApplicationContext
            .javaScriptContextHolder?.get() ?: return
        nativeInstall(jsContext)
    }
}
```

**JNI bridge (cpp/jni.cpp):**
```cpp
extern "C" JNIEXPORT void JNICALL
Java_com_myapp_AudioModule_nativeInstall(JNIEnv* env, jobject thiz, jlong jsiPtr) {
    auto* runtime = reinterpret_cast<facebook::jsi::Runtime*>(jsiPtr);
    install(*runtime);
}
```

**Runtime source (Android):** `JavaScriptContextHolder` → cast `jlong` to `jsi::Runtime*`.

**Gotcha:** Always call `AttachCurrentThread` before any JNI call from a background thread. Never call JNI from a real-time audio thread (JVM may GC).

