## Part 7 — Platform Wiring

### iOS (Objective-C++ / CocoaPods)

**File extension:** `.mm` (Objective-C++) to mix ObjC and C++.

```objc
// ios/AudioModule.mm
#import "AudioModule.h"
#import <React/RCTBridge+Private.h>
#import <jsi/jsi.h>
#include "install.h"  // your C++ install()

@implementation AudioModule

RCT_EXPORT_MODULE()

- (void)setBridge:(RCTBridge *)bridge {
    // Runs after bridge init, before JS evaluation
    RCTCxxBridge *cxxBridge = (RCTCxxBridge *)bridge;
    if (cxxBridge.runtime) {
        install(*(facebook::jsi::Runtime *)cxxBridge.runtime);
    }
}

@end
```

**Podspec** (`AudioModule.podspec`):
```ruby
s.source_files = "ios/**/*.{h,m,mm}", "cpp/**/*.{h,cpp}"
s.dependency "React-Core"
s.dependency "React-jsi"
```

**Runtime source (iOS):** `RCTCxxBridge` — cast `cxxBridge.runtime` to `jsi::Runtime*`.

**Gotcha:** Never send an ObjC message (`[obj method]`) from a real-time audio callback — the ObjC runtime lock causes priority inversion. Use pure C/C++ in real-time threads.

### Android (JNI + CMake)

